    "result_text": "Both tests pass. The full-stack change is complete and verified.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented client tracking (add a client with name + email, list all clients) as an additive full-stack change:\n\n**Database** \u2014 `src/main/resources/db/migration/V1__clients.sql`: new Flyway migration creating a `clients` table (`id`, `name`, `email`), using `GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY` so the test seed can insert explicit fixture ids while normal creates auto-generate.\n\n**Server (OfficeFloor REST + Spring)** \u2014 a self-contained `net.officefloor.hq.app.client` package:\n- `Client` JPA entity + `ClientRepository`\n- `ListClients` logic \u2192 `GET /api/clients` (`clients.GET.yml`)\n- `CreateClient` logic (`NewClient` `@RequestBody`) \u2192 `POST /api/clients` (`clients.POST.yml`)\n\n**Test seed support** \u2014 extended `TestSupportController` (app code, not pinned) to inject `JdbcTemplate`: `reset` now `TRUNCATE TABLE clients RESTART IDENTITY`, and `seed` inserts fixture rows with their explicit ids.\n\n**Front-end** \u2014 implemented the manifest router mechanism in `router/routes.ts` (features auto-discovered via `import.meta.glob`, so pages are new files), wired the nav/page shell in `main.tsx`, and added the `features/clients/feature.tsx` page with the add-client form and the clients list, exposing all the `data-testid` anchors the spec expects (`nav-clients`, `clients-table`, `clients-empty`, `client-row-<id>`, `client-name`, `client-email`, `client-form-name`, `client-form-email`, `client-form-submit`).\n\n`bin/e2e` passes both tests. I didn't touch any pinned scaffolding or the test spec.",
